{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>ki you shall open, etc.</b> One must know what reason this provides for a locked heart. Perhaps it intends to say to him on the basis of what Scripture says (Proverbs 11:24): ״יֵשׁ מְפַזֵּר וְנוֹסָף עוֹד״ — for by opening his hand, the gates of abundance are opened for him. And this is what it says <b>ki</b> — meaning: the reason I am telling you not to harden, etc. — <b>ki you shall open</b>, meaning: the hidden treasure, if you open your hand. And He concludes by saying <b>and you shall lend, etc.</b> — meaning, when you open your hand to him you are doing nothing but a loan specifically, and immediately HaShem will repay you with abundant increase, and in this there is a sound rationale for his heart, that he not harden, etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:31.014527550Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}